All checks pass. Here's a summary of the work:

## Root cause & fix

**`game-src/src/50-main.js`** — the input layer now understands the physical key codes browsers actually send:

| Change | Detail |
|---|---|
| `normalizeCode()` | `KeyW`→`w`, `KeyA`→`a`, `Digit1`→`1`, `Numpad0`→`0`, `Space`→`' '`, `ShiftLeft/Right`→`shift`, `ControlLeft`→`ctrl`, `ArrowUp`→`arrowup` |
| `resolveKey(e.code, e.key)` | prefers the physical key (`e.code`, layout-independent), falls back to `e.key` only when the code isn't mapped |
| `isScrollKey()` | `preventDefault()` only for Space/arrows, now called **before** the `e.repeat` guard so holding Space no longer scrolls the page; letter keys stay unblocked (`Ctrl+F` survives) |
| test contract | `test.key()`/`test.press()` also accept `'KeyW'`; `dbg.normalizeCode/resolveKey/KEY_ACTIONS` exposed. `state`/`test.{key,press,step,teleport,begin,setTime}` unchanged |

## Verification (headless Chrome, real keyboard events)

New `game-src/test/keys.mjs` dispatches **CDP `Input.dispatchKeyEvent`** *and* synthetic `KeyboardEvent`s (code path + key-only path): **33/33 pass**. Run against the pre-fix build it scores 17/33 — reproducing the defect (W/A/S/D `KeyW`→0.000 m, Shift/F/E/R/C/M all dead).

| | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| `KeyW`/`KeyA`/`KeyS`/`KeyD` | 0.000 m | **1.598 m** |
| `ShiftLeft`+`KeyW` | 0.000 m | **6.87 m** (walk 3.70) |
| `KeyF`/`KeyE`/`KeyR`/`KeyC`/`KeyM` | dead | all work |
| `ArrowUp` / `Space` | work | unchanged |

Regression checks: `smoke.mjs` (walk/run/jump/car/drive 61.8 km/h/drift/wanted 1→3/hide/3 missions/time-of-day/AI/police) 0 errors; repo harness `web-tests.mjs` hangang 20/20, palace 7/7, intro 5/5. Docs updated in `HANGANG_README.md`, `WEB_VERIFICATION.md`, `README.md`, and the harness's `FIX_ROUND.md` measurement table.

**Not checked / risks:** `vendor/three.min.js` was stale (r148) while the deliverable embedded r159 and the root build was broken — I replaced the vendored file with the exact r159 payload so `node game-src/build.mjs hangang-city.html` reproduces the 778 KB single-file artifact byte-for-byte; visual output is unchanged (screenshots regenerate identically). Headless Chrome fires a spurious `window.blur` on the first modifier keypress (no window focus); the test uses CDP `Emulation.setFocusEmulationEnabled` to match a real browser, which I could not test on real hardware.
